<title>MALAYSIA: Japan's Daito buys into Malaysian project.</title>
<headline>Japan's Daito buys into Malaysian project.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A subsidiary of Malaysian Resources Corp Bhd (MRCB) has signed an agreement to sell a piece of land to Japan's Daito Trust Construction Co Ltd for 63.4 million ringgit ($25.5 million).</p>
<p>MRCB said in a statement on Thursday that the deal is for Daito to develop a four-star hotel in the Kuala Lumpur Sentral project.  </p>
<p>Daito plans to build the hotel with gross built-up area of 420,000 square feet, the statement said.</p>
<p>MRCB's unit, Kuala Lumpur Sentral Sdn Bhd, is developing the 72-acre site in the Malaysian capital city into a mini-city by 2007.</p>
<p>($1 = 2.49 ringgit)</p>
